  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5f74bbac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Feature 1 — `tenure_group`:** Buckets `tenure` into lifecycle stages (0-12mo, 13-24mo, 25-48mo, 49-60mo, 61-72mo). \n",
    "\n",
    "**Feature 2 — `num_services`:** Counts how many of the 8 available services (phone, multiple lines, online security, backup, device protection, tech support, streaming TV/movies) a customer has subscribed to. 
    "\n",
    "**Feature 3 — `avg_monthly_spend` and `charge_increase`:** `avg_monthly_spend` is `TotalCharges / tenure` (historical average bill). `charge_increase` is `MonthlyCharges − avg_monthly_spend`. *Why useful:* a positive gap signals the customer's **current** bill is higher than their historical average — e.g. a promotional rate just expired — which is a well-known real-world churn trigger that raw `MonthlyCharges` alone can't capture.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
