   "source": [
    "## Train/Test Split & Preprocessing Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "We split **before** fitting any preprocessing, and wrap encoding/scaling inside a `ColumnTransformer` that is fit only on the training set. This guarantees:\n",
    "1. No data leakage from test set statistics into training.\n",
    "2. The exact same transformation can be applied consistently to brand-new customer data at prediction time.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "c0a54fbf",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-05T09:40:21.026350Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-05T09:40:21.026208Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-05T09:40:21.125309Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-05T09:40:21.124377Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Train shape: (4930, 23), Test shape: (2113, 23)\n",
      "Train churn rate: 0.265 | Test churn rate: 0.265\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "X = df.drop(columns=['Churn'])\n",
    "y = df['Churn']\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X, y, test_size=0.30, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, stratify=y\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(f\"Train shape: {X_train.shape}, Test shape: {X_test.shape}\")\n",
    "print(\"Train churn rate:\", y_train.mean().round(3), \"| Test churn rate:\", y_test.mean().round(3))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8b9cf497",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We use `stratify=y` so both train and test sets preserve the same ~26.5% churn rate."
