   "source": [
    "**Comparison & final model selection:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- `DT_shallow_gini_minsplit` has the best precision but the **worst recall (0.45)** — it misses more than half of actual churners, which is risky for a retention use case.\n",
    "- `DT_default_depth5` is well-balanced but still misses ~40% of churners.\n",
    "- `DT_deeper_balanced` trades some precision for a much higher **recall (0.77)** and achieves the best **F1 score**, due to `class_weight='balanced'` explicitly correcting for the 73.5%/26.5% imbalance.\n",
    "\n",
    "**We select `DT_deeper_balanced` as the final model** — both because it has the best F1 score, and because recall matters more than precision for this business problem.\n"
   ]
  },
