  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c302056a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Key findings:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **`Contract_Month-to-month`** is overwhelmingly the most important feature (~50% of total importance) — it's also the very first split at the root of the tree. This confirms the EDA: contract flexibility is the single dominant churn driver.\n",
    "2. **`tenure`** is the second most important feature — consistent with churn being concentrated in a customer's first year.\n",
    "3. **`InternetService_Fiber optic`** ranks third, echoing the EDA finding of elevated fiber churn.\n",
    "4. Our engineered features `charge_increase` and `avg_monthly_spend` both appear in the top 6 — validating that they carry real predictive signal beyond the raw `MonthlyCharges`/`TotalCharges` columns.\n",
    "5. Lack of `TechSupport` and `OnlineSecurity` also contribute meaningfully, reinforcing that \"under-serviced\" customers with no add-ons are more likely to leave.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Overall takeaway:** the customers most worth targeting for retention are **new, month-to-month, fiber-optic customers without tech support/security add-ons, especially if their bill just went up.**\n"
   ]
  },
