   "source": [
    "A REST API (FastAPI) built on top of this saved pipeline is provided separately in `app.py` at the project root, exposing a `POST /predict` endpoint that:\n",
    "1. Accepts raw customer JSON (matching the original Telco schema).\n",
    "2. Validates the input (rejects invalid categories, missing fields, out-of-range values).\n",
    "3. Applies the exact same `engineer_features()` transformation used here.\n",
    "4. Loads the saved pipeline and returns `{\"prediction\": \"Yes\"/\"No\", \"churn_probability\": <float>}`.\n",
    "\n",
    "See the project `README.md` for setup and run instructions, and `sample_request.json` / `sample_response.json` for a worked example.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "## Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "We built a complete churn-prediction workflow: cleaned and understood the data, uncovered clear business drivers of churn through EDA (contract type, tenure, fiber internet, payment method), engineered features that captured lifecycle stage and pricing, trained and compared three Decision Tree configurations, selected a final model justified by the business cost of missing churners (prioritizing recall), interpreted what drives its predictions, and packaged it into a reusable, servable pipeline with a REST API.\n"
   ]
